SRC/knight -- knight, as built for OS-9/68000=============================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.games carried it.  knight.c differsfrom it only inside #ifdef OSK:  - srand48() and lrand48() are srand() and rand(), from /dd/LIB/rand.r.  - OS-9's terminal driver takes ESC as end of file, so `ESC to cancel row'    never arrived: curses read end of file, kept waiting for a column, and    ignored Q.  knight_tty() clears that one setting BEFORE initscr() --    curses rewrites the settings it saved there on every noecho(), and    getrc() calls noecho() for every move -- and knight_endwin() puts back    only that field after endwin().  Measured: ESC re-asks the row, then Q    quits to the shell.